==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{der|fi|gmw-pro|*sunnōn dag}} for sure. Could possibly also be a loan from Old Norse, but sunnuntai matches sunnuntag and sunnundag.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|a=Fi-sunnuntai.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{enum|fi|lauantai|maanantai|day of the week|su}}
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[Sunday]] {{gloss|day of the week; the seventh and last day of the week in Finland and in the ISO 8601 standard}}

====Usage notes====
As with all days of the week in Finnish, the essive case ({{m|fi||sunnuntaina}}) is usually used when talking about what will happen or happened on a Sunday.

====Declension====
